celebrated the birth of कृष्ण as his son by inviting Brahmanas, Gopas and गोपीस् and making rich presents to them, the Gopas and गोपीस् threw balls of turmeric on the baby and sprinkled butter, curds and milk on one another, a folk custom;
3: भा.

-१६; chh. 5. 6, 7 and 8 (whole),
went to मथुरा to pay the annual tribute to Kamsa; was met by Vasudeva who advised him to leave at once for his place as he expected some उत्पातस् there: Nanda thinking Vasu- deva's words to be true turned his thoughts on the way to Hari; heard of पूतना, the demon killed by कृष्ण and felt greatly surprised; embraced कृष्ण in joy; performed शान्ति for कृष्ण for kicking the cart; was surprised at कृष्ण's taking the lap of तृणावर्त and believed more and more in Vasudeva's words; welcomed Garga and had नामकरण done to his sons; became pleased at Garga's service;
3: भा.

-१६; chh. 5. 6, 7 and 8 (whole),
Nanda and his friends bewildered at the fall of the Arjuna trees and released कृष्ण from his fetters; planned to leave Vraja for ब्रिन्दावन;
4: Ib. X. १

; ३६. २४. (३१).
Extended a hearty welcome to अक्रूर and enquired of Kamsa; became afraid of अक्रूर's message; got ready with all the Gopas to start for मथुरा with presents to Kamsa; followed अक्रूर's chariot with all his carts and men; came in advance and waited for कृष्ण's arrival; took his seat along with the other Gopas in the gallery of the wrestling ground; Kamsa desired to imprison him; duly honoured by कृष्ण, Nanda and the Gopas returned to Vraja after Kamsa's death;
9: Ib. X. ३८. ४१-43; ३९. १०-12, ३५; ४१. 8; ४२. ३८; ४४. ३२; ४५. २०-25; Vi. V. ११. 3; १५. १८; २०. २८ and ८३.
welcomed Uddhava with due honour; exhibited his deep love for कृष्ण; Uddhava revealed the real nature of कृष्ण to him.
१०: भा. X. ४६. १४ to the end.
Came to स्यमन्तपञ्चक and met कृष्ण and others; embraced and enquired after by Vasudeva and others;
११: Ib. X. ५२. ३२-35.
was honoured by कृष्ण, राम, Ugrasena and Vasudeva; spent three months unwilling to be away from the Yadus, left for मथुरा;
१२: Ib. X. ८४. ५९-69.
chief of सात्वतस् and vassal of कृष्ण: went with वृष्णिस् to बाण's city.
